   "parts": [
    [
     1,
     "<div dir=\"ltr\">Hi Jason,<div>You can use several different R packages to run Exploratory Factor Analysis (EFA). </div><div>You will see many options if you google EFA in r. </div><div>&quot;psych&quot; package is one of them. Below links are R tutorial for EFA using psych package.</div><div><br></div><div>- <a href=\"http://www.statpower.net/Content/312/R%20Stuff/Exploratory%20Factor%20Analysis%20with%20R.pdf\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"nofollow\" data-saferedirecturl=\"https://www.google.com/url?hl=en-US&amp;q=http://www.statpower.net/Content/312/R%2520Stuff/Exploratory%2520Factor%2520Analysis%2520with%2520R.pdf&amp;source=gmail&amp;ust=1792428085247000&amp;usg=AOvVaw2d6wguXvZ_EtsSAFp31sJ6\">http://www.statpower.net/Content/312/R%20Stuff/Exploratory%20Factor%20Analysis%20with%20R.pdf</a></div><div>- <a href=\"http://rtutorialseries.blogspot.com/2011/10/r-tutorial-series-exploratory-factor.html\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"nofollow\" data-saferedirecturl=\"https://www.google.com/url?hl=en-US&amp;q=http://rtutorialseries.blogspot.com/2011/10/r-tutorial-series-exploratory-factor.html&amp;source=gmail&amp;ust=1792428085247000&amp;usg=AOvVaw2ZtcBzT9z9-zRQd5Ws-8f0\">http://rtutorialseries.blogspot.com/2011/10/r-tutorial-series-exploratory-factor.html</a></div><div><br></div><div>Hope this helps.</div><div><br></div></div><div class=\"gmail_extra\"><br><div class=\"gmail_quote\"></div></div>"
